<Base title="About GuideHollow" description="GuideHollow is an independent English-language resource for understanding AI, writing useful prompts, and building thoughtful everyday workflows." breadcrumbs={[{name:'About',url:'/about/'}]}>
<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ about</p><h1>A clearer path<br />through AI.</h1><p>For people who want to understand what they are using—and make better decisions with it.</p></header><article class="prose info-content"><h2>Why GuideHollow exists</h2><p>AI tools can make everyday work easier, but getting useful results requires more than finding a clever prompt. You need to know what to ask, what information to provide, and what to check before you act on an answer.</p><p>GuideHollow brings those pieces together in plain English. Our guides focus on concrete tasks: explaining an unfamiliar idea, revising an email, checking a formula, or finding the missing assumption in a confident response.</p><h2>What you will find</h2><ul><li>Foundational guides that explain concepts without assuming a technical background.</li><li>Reusable prompts with examples you can adapt to your own work.</li><li>Troubleshooting methods for unreliable answers and overloaded conversations.</li><li>Free browser tools that structure a prompt or guide a careful review.</li></ul><h2>Who is behind the site</h2><p>GuideHollow is an independent project maintained by <a href="https://github.com/emfls">emfls on GitHub</a>. “GuideHollow Editorial” is the site's editorial attribution, not a claim about a staffed newsroom or professional certification. The source code and correction history are available in the <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow">public repository</a>.</p><h2>How we publish</h2><p>Our launch articles were developed with AI assistance and reviewed against the linked official references. We do not present fictional examples as real user stories or claim hands-on tests we have not performed. Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains sourcing, corrections, and limitations.</p><h2>See the work, not just the claims</h2><p>Our explanations distinguish constructed examples, observed model runs, and calculations verified against source data. To see the difference, download the <a href="/examples/weighted-price-sample.csv">original fictional sales CSV</a>, calculate its expected totals in the <a href="/tools/weighted-price-checker/">browser-only audit workbench</a>, and inspect the <a href="/guides/verify-ai-weighted-average-price-spreadsheet/">full spreadsheet methodology</a>. We label fictional transactions as invented rather than presenting them as real customer research or product benchmarks. The <a href="/evidence/">evidence library</a> collects original test fixtures, independent arithmetic controls and documented limitations.</p><h2>Who reviews and corrects the work</h2><p>The public maintainer is the <a href="https://github.com/emfls">emfls GitHub account</a>, linked to the <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow">GuideHollow source repository</a>. GuideHollow Editorial is the name of the publication's editorial responsibility, not a fabricated individual byline, a staffed research institution, or a claim of professional credentials.</p><p>For practical accountability, the <a href="/evidence/">evidence library</a> publishes input data, a reference answer key, negative tests and limitations. The <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow/blob/main/docs/editorial-fact-check-2026-11-01.md">public 31-article review register</a> describes what was examined on November 1 and explicitly identifies historical model and spreadsheet runs we did not independently repeat.</p><p>If you find an incorrect number, outdated product instruction or inaccessible source, send the exact page URL and supporting evidence through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. A correction is only considered resolved when the article and its public change history are updated. This project does not sell consulting, claim certification or charge for its tools.</p><h2>Start somewhere useful</h2><p>Read <a href="/guides/what-is-generative-ai/">what generative AI is</a>, learn <a href="/prompts/how-to-write-better-ai-prompts/">how to write a better prompt</a>, or try the <a href="/tools/ai-prompt-builder/">AI Prompt Builder</a>.</p></article>
</Base>
